-- Installation
   $ sudo apt update
   $ sudo apt install mkcert libnss3-tools -y
   $ mkcert -install

CERTIFICATE ISSUING (wso2 virtual machine)

Since the VM IP may change, we'll use a hostname instead of the IP: wso2.local

-- To create the certificate with mkcert:
   $ mkcert wso2.local

   This generates two files in ~/:
   wso2.local.pem → certificate
   wso2.local-key.pem → private key

-- To convert certificate to PKCS12 (needed for Java)
   $ openssl pkcs12 -export -out wso2.p12 -inkey wso2.local-key.pem \
     \ -in wso2.local.pem -name wso2carbon -password pass:wso2carbon

Make a back-up
   $ mv wso2carbon.jks wso2carbon.jks.bak

